1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,640
Chevron is close to its weekly high.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:05,960
A strong oil tape still leaves an earnings test.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:08,850
The calendar lists earnings Friday before the open.

4
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:15,300
At the October 23 close, Chevron was at $233.21.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:20,740
The weekly low at $221.56 is a support reference.

6
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:25,360
Resistance is near $233.74.

7
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:29,020
Price is above all four averages, with

8
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,200
RSI above seventy.

9
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:33,892
That supports momentum, not a promise of another rise.

10
00:00:34,082 --> 00:00:35,016
RSI is 76.9.

11
00:00:35,016 --> 00:00:38,868
Friday closed near its high, with volume

12
00:00:38,868 --> 00:00:41,842
modestly above average.

13
00:00:41,842 --> 00:00:45,066
Average true range is about $4.78 a day.

14
00:00:45,066 --> 00:00:48,706
It describes recent movement, not a limit

15
00:00:48,706 --> 00:00:50,100
on an earnings gap.

16
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:53,743
Zacks projects $4.78 in quarterly earnings per

17
00:00:53,743 --> 00:00:57,290
share, more than twice the year earlier figure.

18
00:00:57,290 --> 00:01:00,314
Recent coverage also highlights a potential one

19
00:01:00,314 --> 00:01:03,610
time charge linked to Hess Midstream restructuring.

20
00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:07,434
Separate accounting items from production, operating cash

21
00:01:07,434 --> 00:01:10,183
flow and the benefits of higher oil prices.

22
00:01:10,373 --> 00:01:14,110
The October 30 at-the-money straddle midpoint gives

23
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:17,333
a rough 3.9 percent move in either direction.

24
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:20,373
It covers risk through expiry, not just

25
00:01:20,373 --> 00:01:23,266
earnings, and the actual move can be larger.

26
00:01:23,457 --> 00:01:32,297
Holding $221.56 and reclaiming $233.74 would improve the chart.

27
00:01:32,297 --> 00:01:34,857
A break below support would weaken it.

28
00:01:34,857 --> 00:01:38,097
Watch the reaction and volume after the report.

29
